\tr{\td{reference engine by name, 4 workers}\td{cslib, navier-stokes-euler, con-leche}\td{1,249.5 M}\td{250.7 M}\td{160}\td{1,470}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{\strong{all 44 runs}}\td{}\td{\strong{2,851.0 M}}\td{\strong{444.2 M}}\td{\strong{5,516}}\td{\strong{20,761}}\td{\strong{0}}}
}

\p{Every run accepted its corpus. The twin is the code the release runs; the base it reads is the snapshot the loader froze, so the comparison covers the lookups, the caches and their stamps, the memos and the reset and rebase of the new layout under the schedules of real runs. It does not cover the loader's own store, which did not change kind.}
}

